<title>SWITZERLAND: U.S. submits new offer in WTO telecom talks.</title>
<headline>U.S. submits new offer in WTO telecom talks.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States on Wednesday submitted a new and improved offer in World Trade Organisation talks on a global pact to open telecommunications markets, WTO officials said.</p>
<p>The move followed similar action on Tuesday by the European Union, which said it was working together with the United States to give impetus to the negotiations aimed at shaping a WTO deal by next February 15.</p>
<p>There was no immediate information on the content of the U.S. offer, which was put in despite a Supreme Court ruling in Washington on Tuesday which trade analysts said cast doubt on how far U.S. commitments on market openings could go.</p>
</text>
